request:
an ordinary put, sent while a watch on `wk` is open

POST /v3/kv/put
{
  "key": "d2s=",
  "value": "djE="
}

response:
the put's own header — and, on the open stream, one event at that revision

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "header": {
    "cluster_id": "8120124649628684138",
    "member_id": "4254765522799318016",
    "raft_term": "2",
    "revision": "2"
  }
}

request:
the delete of the same key, again with a watch open

POST /v3/kv/deleterange
{
  "key": "d2s="
}

response:
`deleted: 1` here, and a second event on the stream

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "deleted": "1",
  "header": {
    "cluster_id": "3327965217934999551",
    "member_id": "13214582014237292270",
    "raft_term": "2",
    "revision": "3"
  }
}
